Jesus returned to the vicinity of Lake Galilee, where people gathered around him, and he began teaching them.
And Levi was sitting at the tax office when Jesus saw him; so he said to him, "Follow me." And he got up and followed him.
While Jesus was eating in Levi's house, many tax collectors and sinners were also sitting with him and his disciples because there were many who followed him.
When they saw that he was eating with tax collectors and sinners, his disciples said to him, "Why do you eat with tax collectors and sinners?"
And when he heard it, Jesus said to them, "Those who are well have no need of a physician, but those who are sick; I came not to call the righteous, but sinners." Question about fasting
John's disciples and the Pharisees were fasting, so they came to Jesus and asked, "Why do John's disciples and the Pharisees fast, but your disciples don't?"
Jesus answered them, "How can wedding guests fast while the groom is with them? They cannot fast as long as they have the groom with them."
But one day, the groom will be chosen from among them, and that's when they'll all cry.
Even if you patch an old piece of clothing with new fabric, it will shrink when washed and make the tear bigger.
Even one who puts new wine in old wineskins is condemned; for the new wine will burst the skins, and it will be spilled, and the skins will be destroyed. But new wine must be put into fresh wineskins." And he was teaching in their synagogues throughout all Judea and Samaria.
And one Saturday # 2:23 which is the day of rest and worship for Jews
The Pharisees came to him and said, "Why do your disciples break the Sabbath rules by doing what isn't allowed on that day?" Jesus went through the fields of grain, and his disciples began plucking heads of wheat as they walked along.
Jesus replied to them, "Haven't you read what David did when he was hungry? He went into God's house while Abiathar was high priest."
And how did he enter the house of God? And why did Abiathar, who was chief priest at that time, give him bread from the holy offerings which were reserved for priests alone, except when they offered sacrifices to God? And why did he also share it with his companions?"
He said to them, "The Sabbath was made for man, not man for the Sabbath."
But the Son of Man is Lord even of the Sabbath.»
Chapter 3 Jesus heals on the Sabbath
And Jesus went again into the temple; and there was a man with his hand withered.
The Pharisees were watching Jesus closely to see if he would heal someone on the Sabbath so they could accuse him.
Jesus said to the man whose hand was paralyzed, "Get up and stand in front!"
And he said to the Pharisees, "Which is lawful on the Sabbath: to do good or to do evil, to save life or to kill?" But they remained silent.
He looked at them angrily and was deeply saddened by their cruelty. He said to the man, "Give me your hand!" And he gave him his hand, which was trembling.
The Pharisees went away and started plotting with the Herodians how to kill Jesus. Many people were following Jesus.
Jesus went with his disciples to the other side of Lake Galilee, and there followed him many people from Galilee and Judea.
From Jerusalem and Idumea, from beyond the Jordan and around Tyre and Sidon, great crowds came to hear him and be healed of their diseases.
He told his disciples to get him a boat so that people wouldn't crowd around him, Mark
He healed many people, so much that sick people started crowding around him to touch him.
And those who were possessed with demons saw Jesus fall at his feet and cried out in fear: "What do you have to do with us, Son of God?"
But Jesus warned them and emphasized that they should not tell anyone who he is. Jesus chose the apostles from among ordinary people.
He went up to one man and called for his men, who came running towards him.
He chose twelve men whom he called apostles to be with him and send them forth to preach the good news.
And they have the power to bring madness.
And this one is called Simon, whom Jesus named Peter.
Jacob son of Zebedee and his brother John, whom Jesus called Boanerges, which means "sons of thunder."
Andras, Philip, Bartholomew, Matthew, Thomas, James son of Alphaeus, Thaddeus, Simon the Zealot
Judas Iscariot who will betray Jesus. Jesus and Beelzebul
After that, Jesus went to someone's house where crowds gathered around him so much that he couldn't even eat with his disciples.
And when Jesus' family heard about it, they said, "He has lost his mind!"
The teachers of religious law who came from Jerusalem said to him, "Why does your disciple cast out demons by Beelzebul, the prince of demons?" Matthew
Jesus wept over the teachers of the law and spoke to them in parables, saying: "How can Satan cast out Satan?"
Except for one kingdom that is divided and its people fight among themselves, such a kingdom cannot be stable.
Otherwise, if it's a family that divides and quarrels among themselves, then this family won't be able to stay together.
